  "tolerancePolicy": "Seeded 2026-08-10 from the recorded fidelity run (geometry/edge/material measured vs the pinned references, margin x1.5/x1.4 + 0.02/0.5/5). The gate catches regressions beyond this recorded baseline; P1 fidelity work tightens these values toward the historical targets. Platinum icon material is looser (110) because the painter palette is still being calibrated; its silhouette (geometry/edge) stays strict. A specimen with tolerances:null stays diagnostic-only. Two tiers, never merged: `tolerances` is the regression tier (seeded from the recorded run with a margin, so it detects drift from that run — not distance from the historical target). `floor` is the absolute tier from FIDELITY_FLOOR in tooling/theme-lab-fidelity-contract.mjs (geometry 0.05, edge 1.5px at 1x scaled by deviceScaleFactor, material 12); it is identical for every era and never derived from our own output. Every specimen must meet the floor unless its ledger names the metric under `failing` (a real gap, with its historical reason) or `exempt` (the pinned crop cannot support that metric). A `failing` metric that starts to meet the floor fails the gate until the ledger is corrected, so an improvement cannot hide behind a stale entry."
}
